                                                             "tags":  "A melancholic and emotionally dark Japanese rock song titled \"Liar\". The song begins with a cold, sorrowful piano melody, minimal and delicate, setting a mood of quiet despair. Clean electric guitar with delay joins subtly, supporting a soft and fragile male vocal singing about the pain of seeing through lies. The chorus introduces gentle overdrive guitar and emotional drums, but keeps a somber, introspective atmosphere. Piano arpeggios remain throughout, carrying a sense of sadness and inevitability. Strings swell in the bridge for emotional intensity, then the last chorus peaks with restrained but powerful energy. The track ends with a lonely, fading piano. Minor key, tempo around 90 BPM. Inspired by dark emotional anime rock like unravel. No cheerful or bright tones—keep the tone cold, tragic, and haunting.",
